# Rule: testing

Tests are evidence. A test that cannot fail proves nothing.

## Layers
| Layer | Proves | Where | Runs in |
|---|---|---|---|
| Unit | one behaviour, fast, no network/disk | `<%#hasBackend%><%backendDir%>/tests/<%/hasBackend%>`<%#hasWeb%>, `<%webDir%>/src/__tests__/`<%/hasWeb%> | `gates` |
| Contract | the API shape did not drift | `backend.contract` gate | `gates` |
| Facts | each PRD acceptance criterion holds on the RUNNING system | `.ai/specs/*/acceptance.json` | `facts` |

## Standards
- Coverage floors are enforced, not advisory:<%#hasBackend%> backend >= <%coverageBackend%>%<%/hasBackend%><%#hasWeb%>, web >= <%coverageWeb%>%<%/hasWeb%>. Never lower them to pass.
- Arrange / Act / Assert. One reason to fail per test. Name tests by behaviour: `test_hello_rejects_name_longer_than_50_chars`.
- Cover: happy path, every validation rule, boundaries (0, 1, max, max+1), error paths, and each acceptance criterion at least once.
- Deterministic: no sleeping, no real clock/network/randomness without control. Fakes at the system boundary only; do not mock the unit under test.
- Test first for new behaviour: write the failing test, watch it fail for the right reason, then make it pass.
- A bug fix starts with a test that reproduces the bug.
- Never `skip`, `xfail`, `.only`, or delete a test to get green.
